{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 48,
  "title": "In the countryside",
  "description": "Name the things outside the town, and say where they are.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Outside the town the vocabulary opens up: fields, rivers, hills and animals. The grammar is the one you already know.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "El campo, el bosque, el río, el monte, el caballo y la abeja are masculine. La granja, la piedra y la oveja are feminine. El campo is the countryside and the field at the same time, and el monte is a hill or a mountain.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el campo",
            "en": "the countryside"
          },
          {
            "es": "la granja",
            "en": "the farm"
          },
          {
            "es": "la oveja",
            "en": "the sheep"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where they are",
        "body": "Estar says where a thing is, and outside the town you use it with big places: el caballo está en el campo, la granja está cerca del río. En el campo and en la granja are the two you will use most.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "la abeja está en la flor",
            "en": "the bee is on the flower"
          },
          {
            "es": "el caballo está en el campo",
            "en": "the horse is in the field"
          },
          {
            "es": "hay una piedra en el camino",
            "en": "there is a stone on the path"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
